From: linux-omarchy-aarch64
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: x1-asus-vivobook-s15: let the panel 3.3 V
 switch off

VREG_EDP_3P3 only feeds the Samsung ATNA56AC03 panel, and the panel
node already names it as power-supply, so the panel driver enables it
while the display is on. regulator-always-on kept that rail up through
s2idle. Drop it and keep regulator-boot-on so the bootloader handoff
stays seamless.

The node lives in x1-asus-vivobook-s15.dtsi, which both the X1E80100
and X1P42100 Vivobook S 15 trees include. Other laptops are unchanged.

Source: https://github.com/justririll/x1e-sleep/blob/4e84b60eb0/vivobook-s15/kernel/dts-vivobook-s15-edp-regulator-not-always-on.patch
On that tree, removing the flag cut s2idle from about 1.43 W to about
0.25 W.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-asus-vivobook-s15.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-asus-vivobook-s15.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-asus-vivobook-s15.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-asus-vivobook-s15.dtsi
@@ -177,7 +177,6 @@ vreg_edp_3p3: regulator-edp-3p3 {
 		pinctrl-0 = <&edp_reg_en>;
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 
-		regulator-always-on;
 		regulator-boot-on;
 	};
 
